+# Reader-Supplied Filter Values Do Not Become Cache Keys
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+Both read methods on the veterinarian repository are cached under the `vets` cache, and that cache declares neither an eviction policy nor a size limit — [Open Questions](../system-design.md#open-questions-from-the-survey) records the missing eviction as unsettled. Today that is harmless because both key spaces are fixed and small: one entry for the whole collection, one per requested page.
+
+Specialty narrowing ([`REQ-VET-004`](../prd.md#req-vet-004)) adds reads whose argument comes from the request. Caching them the same way is the obvious move, because every neighbouring method carries the annotation. It would make an arbitrary caller's text the cache key. There is no authentication anywhere in the application (`NG-1`), so any caller can mint entries in an unbounded, never-evicted cache.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Cache the narrowed reads under `vets`** — symmetric with the neighbours, and unbounded in an unauthenticated application.
+2. **Cache them under a separate cache with a size limit and eviction** — bounds the growth, at the cost of settling sizing and eviction that nothing has settled yet.
+3. **Leave the narrowed reads uncached** — the database answers every narrowed request.
+
+## Decision
+
+Option 3. A repository read whose result depends on a reader-supplied value is not cached. Caching stays on the two methods whose key spaces are fixed.
+
+Option 2 is the answer if narrowed reads ever need caching, but it requires the eviction and sizing decisions that remain open, and it buys little against a seeded three-row specialty table.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Every narrowed request reaches the database. For a directory of this size that is a single indexed join, and the unnarrowed paths readers hit by default stay cached.
+- The rule generalizes past this feature: while the cache is unbounded and the application unauthenticated, request input does not reach a cache key.
+- A contributor adding the annotation to a narrowed finder for symmetry reintroduces the growth. [system-design.md § Threat Model](../system-design.md#threat-model) carries the row so a reviewer meets it there.
+- The cached key spaces stay enumerable, so the open question about vet cache invalidation keeps the scope it already had.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VET-004
+
+## References
+
+- [system-design.md § Threat Model](../system-design.md#threat-model) — the row this decision mitigates
+- [system-design.md § Open Questions from the Survey](../system-design.md#open-questions-from-the-survey) — the unsettled vet cache eviction
+- [ADR: Specialty Narrowing Reuses Both Veterinarian Routes as an Optional Parameter](2026-08-07-specialty-narrowing-on-existing-vet-routes.md) — the contract that introduces the reader-supplied value
