+# Specialty Narrowing Reuses Both Veterinarian Routes as an Optional Parameter
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+> **Decided 2026-08-07 by the product owner.** The external contract below is stated intent, not reconstruction.
+
+## Context
+
+[`REQ-VET-004`](../prd.md#req-vet-004) narrows either published form of the veterinarian directory to one specialty. Two forms already exist: the paged HTML directory and the machine-readable list reinstated as [`REQ-VET-003`](../prd.md#req-vet-003).
+
+The PRD states behavior and by its own convention keeps URLs and parameter names out. The narrowing is an external contract that callers bookmark and link, so it needs a home; this ADR is it. [`system-design.md`](../system-design.md#contracts) names the contracts and back-links here rather than transcribing the literals.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **A second route per form** — a narrowed route alongside each published one. Doubles the surface and leaves two handlers per form to keep in step.
+2. **A path segment carrying the specialty** — reads well for one value, but the unnarrowed and narrowed forms then differ in shape, and an absent value has no natural spelling.
+3. **An optional query parameter on both existing routes** — one handler per form, one shape, absence spelled by omission.
+
+## Decision
+
+Option 3. Both existing veterinarian routes take an optional `specialty` query parameter.
+
+- `/vets.html?specialty=<name>` renders the directory page over the narrowed list. Paging applies to the narrowed list, not to the whole one.
+- `/vets?specialty=<name>` returns the machine-readable list narrowed the same way.
+- The value matches a whole specialty name, disregarding letter case. A value matching only the start of a name matches no veterinarian.
+- An absent, empty, or all-spaces value leaves the form unnarrowed, the way an empty owner search returns every owner.
+- A value no veterinarian holds yields the ordinary page or document carrying no veterinarian, not a failure.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- No new entry point is added, which is the ground [the non-goal ADR](2026-08-07-non-goal-veterinarian-search.md) draws its line on: the reader picks from a bounded set the page already prints.
+- Paging links must carry the parameter, or paging past the first page silently drops the narrowing. They are built with Thymeleaf's URL builder so the reader's value is encoded rather than concatenated into the link.
+- Reader-supplied text now reaches the persistence query and the rendered page. Its route into the cache is settled separately by [Reader-Supplied Filter Values Do Not Become Cache Keys](2026-08-07-reader-supplied-values-are-not-cache-keys.md).
+- Matching disregards letter case in the query itself rather than relying on a column type or collation. Owner search took the other path and matches case-sensitively under PostgreSQL as a result — recorded under [Known Defects](../system-design.md#known-defects).
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VET-003, REQ-VET-004
+
+## References
+
+- [system-design.md § Contracts](../system-design.md#contracts) — the veterinarian contracts this shapes
+- [prd.md § Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#veterinarian-directory) — the behavior this serves
+- [ADR: Veterinarian Free-Text Search Stays a Non-Goal, Specialty Filtering Does Not](2026-08-07-non-goal-veterinarian-search.md) — why the narrowing is in scope at all
